{"indicator":"minimum-wage-usd","unit":"美元/月","years":[1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024],"latestWithin":3,"notes":{"KHM":"柬埔寨的最低工資是用美元訂的（成衣、製鞋業），ILOSTAT 誤當成瑞爾換算，這裡改回原本的美元金額","LBN":"ILOSTAT 2020–2023 年用官方匯率換算（2020–2022 年 1 美元 = 1,507.5 鎊，2023 年平均約 13,900 鎊），市場匯率早已貶到幾萬鎊，所以這幾年不列美元值","IRN":"ILOSTAT 2001 年以前用 1 美元 = 1,750 里亞爾的官方匯率換算（2002 年匯率並軌後是 6,900），2018 年起又用42,000 里亞爾的官方匯率（只用於部分必需品進口），市場匯率 2023 年已經貶到 50 萬里亞爾左右。這樣最低工資會被高估好幾倍（2023 年變成 1,264 美元），所以這些年不列美元值；購買力平價不受影響","IDN":"ILOSTAT 的印尼原本是各省最低工資的中位數（2022 年 2,679,815 盧比），2023、2024 年卻變成最高的雅加達（4,901,798、5,067,381 盧比），前後不可比，所以這兩年不列","SYR":"ILOSTAT 的敘利亞最低工資多年沒有更新（2013–2022 年都是 9,765 鎊，實際上 2021 年已經調到 71,515 鎊、年底再調到 92,970 鎊），2010 年以前又用每美元 11.2 鎊的舊官方匯率換算（實際約 50 鎊），所以全部不列","CHE":"瑞士沒有全國的最低工資，只有 5 個州自己訂；ILOSTAT 2020 年起用的是日內瓦州的（2023 年每小時 24 法郎，以每週 40 小時換算成每月 4,157 法郎），2017 年是紐沙特爾州的，都不代表全國","ISL":"冰島沒有法定最低工資，ILOSTAT 用的是勞資協約訂的最低工資；冰島的協約依法適用於同行業的所有勞工","SDN":"蘇丹的一般最低工資 2013 年起一直是每月 425 鎊，沒有隨物價調整，2021 年匯率放寬後只值 1 美元左右（公務員的最低工資 2020 年調到 3,000 鎊）","TWN":"ILOSTAT 沒有台灣，改用勞動部公告的每月基本工資（2025 年起改稱最低工資），取每年 7 月 1 日適用的金額（ILOSTAT 對年中調整的國家也是這樣取），用中央銀行的年平均匯率換算。2024 年 27,470 元、2025 年 28,590 元、2026 年 29,500 元；勞動部 2026-10-16 公告 2027 年 1 月 1 日起每月 30,900 元、每小時 205 元"},"notesEn":{"KHM":"Cambodia sets its minimum wage in US dollars (garment and footwear sector); ILOSTAT converts it as if it were in riels, so the original dollar amount is used here","LBN":"ILOSTAT converts 2020–2023 at the official exchange rate (1,507.5 pounds per US dollar in 2020–2022, about 13,900 on average in 2023), long after the market rate collapsed to tens of thousands of pounds, so US dollar values for those years are left out","IRN":"ILOSTAT converts at the official rate of 1,750 rials per US dollar up to 2001 (6,900 after the rates were unified in 2002) and at the official rate of 42,000 rials from 2018 (used only for some essential imports), while the market rate had fallen to around 500,000 rials by 2023. This overstates the minimum wage several times over (US$1,264 in 2023), so US dollar values for those years are left out; the PPP values are not affected","IDN":"ILOSTAT's figure for Indonesia was the median of the provincial minimum wages (2,679,815 rupiah in 2022), but for 2023 and 2024 it is Jakarta's, the highest (4,901,798 and 5,067,381 rupiah). As the two are not comparable, 2023 and 2024 are left out","SYR":"ILOSTAT's minimum wage for Syria has not been updated for years (9,765 pounds throughout 2013–2022, although it was raised to 71,515 pounds in 2021 and to 92,970 at the end of that year), and years up to 2010 are converted at an old official rate of 11.2 pounds per US dollar (about 50 in practice), so all years are left out","CHE":"Switzerland has no national minimum wage, only five cantons set their own. From 2020 ILOSTAT uses Geneva's (24 francs an hour in 2023, or 4,157 francs a month at 40 hours a week) and for 2017 Neuchâtel's, so the figure does not represent the whole country","ISL":"Iceland has no statutory minimum wage; ILOSTAT uses the minimum set in collective agreements, which by law apply to all workers in the sector","SDN":"Sudan's general minimum wage has stayed at 425 pounds a month since 2013 without adjusting for inflation, so it was worth about one US dollar after the exchange rate was floated in 2021 (the minimum for civil servants was raised to 3,000 pounds in 2020)","TWN":"Taiwan is not in ILOSTAT; the monthly basic wage announced by the Ministry of Labor (called the minimum wage from 2025) used instead, taking the amount in force on 1 July of each year (as ILOSTAT does for countries that change it mid-year), converted at the Central Bank annual average exchange rate. NT$27,470 in 2024, NT$28,590 in 2025, NT$29,500 in 2026; on 2026-10-16 the Ministry of Labor announced NT$30,900 a month and NT$205 an hour from 2027-01-01"},"encoding":"delta","values":{"AFG":[-1,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,nu